<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Christmas Programs and Holiday Outings: Van Rentals for Church and Community Groups</h1>
<p>December is the busiest month on a church calendar. One van keeps the whole group together.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>December fills up fast for churches, schools, and community groups. Caroling at the nursing home, a youth group trip to a Christmas concert, the choir's program at a sister church across the county, a staff outing to see the lights. Every one of those trips is easier when the whole group rides together instead of in a parade of carpools.</p>
<h2>The right van for the group</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Up to 15 people:</strong> our <a href="/van-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">15-passenger van</a> is $135/day plus $0.10/mile, or $750/week with unlimited miles for local renters. We have one, so book it early.</li>
<li><strong>Up to 7 people:</strong> the <a href="/blog/7-passenger-minivan-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">7-passenger minivan</a> is $78/day plus $0.10/mile, or $450/week with unlimited miles for local renters. It's easier to park and to drive in snow.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What a December outing costs</h2>
<p>A choir trip of 60 miles round trip in the 15-passenger van comes to $135 plus $6 in mileage: about $141 before taxes and fees. Split across 12 singers, that's under $12 a person. A two-day retreat of 200 total miles comes to $270 plus $20. The <a href="/blog/15-passenger-van-rental-cost-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">15-passenger cost guide</a> has more worked examples.</p>
<h2>Who drives, and whose insurance</h2>
<p>The driver needs to be 21 or older with a valid U.S. driver's license. The renter brings a Visa, Mastercard, or Discover credit or debit card linked to a checking account, and proof of full-coverage auto insurance. Riverside doesn't sell insurance. If your church or organization has its own policy, ask your agent whether it covers a rented 15-passenger van. That's the vehicle type where the answer most often changes. Our <a href="/blog/does-car-insurance-cover-rental-car-wisconsin.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">insurance guide</a> lists the questions to ask.</p>
<h2>Driving a big van in winter</h2>
<p>Give yourself more time and more room. A full 15-passenger van needs longer to stop than a car, takes wider turns, and catches wind on open stretches of I-94. Check <a href="https://511wi.gov" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;" rel="noopener">511 Wisconsin</a> before you leave, keep speeds down on snowy roads, and plan your parking at the venue ahead of time.</p>
<p><strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> to put your group's date on the calendar. Our hours are Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, Saturday 8:00 AM to noon, and Sunday closed. After-hours drop-off returns are available.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How much does it cost to rent a van for a church group outing?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>The 15-passenger van is $135/day plus $0.10/mile, or $750/week with unlimited miles for local renters. A 60-mile round trip comes to about $141 before taxes and fees. The 7-passenger minivan is $78/day plus $0.10/mile.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Who can drive the 15-passenger van?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Drivers must be 21 or older with a valid U.S. driver&#x27;s license. There is no young-driver fee.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Does our church&#x27;s insurance cover a rented 15-passenger van?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>It depends on the policy. Ask your agent specifically about a rented 15-passenger van. Riverside Auto Rental doesn&#x27;t sell insurance, and the renter must bring proof of full-coverage auto insurance.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How far ahead should we book a van for December?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>As early as you can. There is one 15-passenger van in the fleet, and December weekends book up with church, school, and family trips.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
